    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, led by **Kyle Tucker** (77.32) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset, benefiting from a +17% boost due to a soft matchup against Lorenzen, while **Jackson Merrill** mirrors that efficiency despite a matchup against Gallen; his score is buoyed by a +19% SP skill advantage and a stolen base environment where the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery significantly increases his upside. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55) and **Andy Pages** (71.34) anchor the top of our lineup, both capitalizing on favorable platoon advantages and favorable order slots. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is particularly noteworthy, as his strong dynamic platoon profile against Imai makes him a primary source of run production today.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Jorge Polanco** (55.28) on the bench. While his score is respectable, he was narrowly edged out by the superior platoon profiles of **Curtis Mead** (60.76) and **Nasim Nunez** (60.95), who both benefit from the defensive and delivery-related vulnerabilities of Imai. **Nasim Nunez** remains a vital inclusion given our focus on the scarce stolen base category, as his ability to capitalize on Imai's slow delivery outweighs the marginal points lost by his lower spot in the batting order. We are maintaining a cautious watch on **Gunnar Henderson** (57.32) and **Coby Mayo** (56.35); while both occupy key slots, they face a 45% rain risk in their matchup against Boyd, which could curtail their opportunities to impact the scoreboard. Furthermore, **Drake Baldwin** (43.62) faces a daunting challenge against Skenes and carries a 33% rain risk, leaving him as a marginal start that we will monitor closely as lineups and weather conditions stabilize.",
